Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-01
Subject: Avoid packed lvalue hazards in the translated bootstrap
License: expat

tp2cc can safely lower scalar reads through packed subrecords, but it still
must not bind C++ references to packed storage for mutable lvalues, indexed
aggregate elements, or `var`-like updates.

Keep serialized/on-disk records packed, but route the remaining unsafe access
patterns through aligned carriers.  Use an explicit typed pointer carrier for
PE optional-header `DataDirectory` indexing.  Copy packed `init_settings`
fields before passing them to setter `var` parameters.  Copy
`init_settings.alignment` before mutating its fields and assign the whole
subrecord back.  Copy the scanner's `current_settings` fields before passing
them to the same setter family.

For in-memory-only metadata, remove unnecessary packing in
`compiler/i386/daopt386.pas` optimizer `TContent` and
`compiler/x86/aasmcpu.pas` `TInsProp` / `tinsentry`.

This does not change PPU or object-file formats. It only avoids forming C++
references to misaligned packed subobjects in the translated bootstrap.

--- a/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
